The src/native files were extracted from LocalViewer's native conversion code.
Changes include removal of Android/JNI presentation and entry points, portable
C++ interfaces, source-preservation validation, and host build integration.
The conversion option contracts follow StillExport.kt, StillExportQuality.kt,
RawExportControls.kt, and ImageConversionPreferences.kt.

Codec libraries are downloaded or supplied separately and retain their own
licenses and notices: libultrahdr (Apache-2.0/MIT), libjpeg-turbo (IJG/BSD/zlib),
libjxl and skcms (BSD/Apache-2.0 and accompanying dependency notices), libavif
(BSD), libaom (BSD and patent license), LibRaw (LGPL/CDDL), jxrlib (BSD), libpng (libpng license), zlib (zlib license), libwebp (BSD
and patent license), libtiff (libtiff license), stb_image (MIT/public domain),
OpenEXR/Imath (BSD-3-Clause), and OpenEXR's bundled libdeflate (MIT),
OpenJPH (BSD-2-Clause), and Zstandard (BSD-3-Clause).
Consult each dependency's license files when distributing binaries and source.

COPYING retains GPL version 3 for distributions combined with Exiv2; it is not
the license of the project's original source code.
The native converter links Exiv2 (GPL and accompanying dependency notices) for
photographic metadata. The optional desktop links Qt 6 Widgets
(LGPL/GPL/commercial licensing). The pinned Ultra HDR CPU-count
helper is adapted in a generated build-tree copy to honor per-conversion thread
budgets; its original licenses and notices are retained.

HDR PNG source support follows LocalViewer commit
bbbeba5db374936c624951e491cc7b828397d673, adapted for the portable libpng
decoder, float32 processing and source-preserving JXL/AVIF exports.

Native HEIC decoding uses libheif and libde265 (LGPL v3 or later). Apple and
ProXDR gain-map interpretation follows LocalViewer's HeifContainer.kt,
AppleGainMapDecode.kt, SourceEncodedResult.kt and OppoProxdr.kt, with native
integer RGB decoding and MakerNote-local byte-order handling. The libde265
"dist" convenience target is namespaced during configuration to coexist with
libaom; decoding code is unchanged.
Ultra HDR's generated build-tree appendGainMap implementation emits ISO-only
metadata when a map cannot be represented by its XMP writer (per-channel values
or alternate application space); compatible maps still receive both packets.
